details:
(a) whether Government has reviewed recent geopolitical developments in the Indo-Pacific region and their implications for India's maritime security and trade interests;
(b) whether India has strengthened strategic cooperation with friendly countries to ensure secure sea lanes and regional stability;
(c) the measures taken to safeguard India's maritime economic interests through diplomatic engagement; and
(d) whether Government proposes to further enhance India's role in regional maritime cooperation initiatives?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the increasing pendency of civil and criminal cases in subordinate courts across Bihar;
(b) whether shortages of judicial officers, court infrastructure and digital facilities have contributed to delays in justice delivery;
(c) the measures taken in coordination with the State Government to improve judicial infrastructure and case management systems; and
(d) whether a time-bound action plan has been prepared to reduce pendency in Bihar's subordinate courts?

(a) whether Government has assessed the availability and quality of telecom and broadband connectivity in the Aspirational Districts of Bihar;
(b) whether inadequate digital infrastructure continues to affect education, healthcare, governance and financial inclusion in these districts;
(c) the measures taken to improve mobile coverage, optical fibre connectivity and digital infrastructure in underserved areas; and
(d) whether a time-bound plan has been prepared to achieve universal digital connectivity in the State?

(a) whether Government has identified accident-prone stretches on National Highways passing through Bihar based on recent road accident data;
(b) whether road engineering deficiencies and inadequate safety infrastructure continue to contribute to fatal accidents in the State;
(c) the measures taken to improve highway design, emergency trauma response and intelligent traffic management systems; and
(d) whether a time-bound programme has been prepared to eliminate black spots on National Highways in Bihar?
GK

(a) whether Government has undertaken a review of the functioning and regulation of coaching institutions preparing students for national competitive examinations;
(b) whether the absence of uniform standards has affected student welfare, transparency and quality of education;
(c) the measures taken to establish minimum academic, safety and counselling standards for coaching centres; and
(d) whether Government proposes to evolve a national regulatory framework for coaching institutions?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive review of freight rail infrastructure to improve logistics efficiency and reduce transportation costs;
(b) whether congestion on major freight corridors continues to affect industrial supply chains and export competitiveness;
(c) the measures taken to expand multimodal freight terminals, automate cargo handling and modernise railway logistics systems; and
(d) whether a long term strategy has been formulated to increase the share of railways in the national freight movement?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive review of resilience of India's telecom infrastructure against cyber-attacks, network failures and natural disasters;
(b) whether existing telecom security standards are adequate to address emerging technological threats;
(c) the measures taken to improve network redundancy, emergency communication systems and infrastructure resilience; and
(d) whether a national telecom resilience policy is under consideration?

(a) whether Government has assessed the socio-economic impact of large-scale migration of skilled and semi-skilled workers from Bihar to other States;
(b) whether sector-wise studies have identified the principal causes of outward migration and labour shortages within the State;
(c) the measures taken to promote high-quality employment opportunities, industrial workforce development and skill retention in the State; and
(d) whether Government proposes to formulate a coordinated strategy with State Governments to address regional labour migration?

(a) whether Government has reviewed India's progress in quantum computing, quantum communication and quantum sensing technologies;
(b) whether research institutions possess adequate scientific infrastructure and skilled manpower to compete globally;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen industry-academia collaboration and indigenous technology development in the quantum sector; and
(d) whether a long-term roadmap has been prepared to position India as a global leader in quantum technologies?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the road infrastructure required to support multimodal logistics parks, industrial corridors and freight movement in Bihar;
(b) whether inadequate highway connectivity continues to constrain industrial investment and agricultural supply chains in the State;
(c) the measures taken to integrate National Highways with railway freight terminals, inland waterways and industrial clusters in Bihar; and
(d) whether any comprehensive logistics corridor development plan has been prepared for the State?

(a) whether Government has examined the increasing use of Artificial Intelligence in banking, insurance and financial markets for lending, fraud detection and investment decisions;
(b) whether adequate regulatory safeguards exist to address algorithmic bias, data privacy and systemic financial risks arising from AI-based financial services;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen supervisory mechanisms for emerging financial technologies; and
(d) whether a comprehensive regulatory framework is under consideration for responsible adoption of Artificial Intelligence in the financial sector?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the growing use of deceptive online interface designs, commonly known as 'Dark Patterns', affecting consumer choice on digital platforms;
(b) whether complaints relating to misleading subscription models, hidden charges and manipulative consent mechanisms have increased in recent years;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen consumer protection and transparency in digital marketplaces; and
(d) whether further regulatory interventions are under consideration to prevent unfair digital trade practices?

(a) whether Government has assessed the requirement for dedicated air cargo infrastructure in the State of Bihar to facilitate transportation of agricultural produce, horticultural products, fisheries and other perishable commodities to domestic and international markets;
(b) whether the absence of integrated cold-chain and air cargo facilities at airports in the State has affected export competitiveness and farmers' income;
(c) measures taken to strengthen air freight terminals, cold storage facilities and multimodal logistics connectivity in the State; and
(d) whether Government proposes to develop the State of Bihar as an air cargo hub for agricultural exports from eastern India?

(a) whether Government has assessed the increasing passenger and freight traffic on major railway corridors passing through Bihar, particularly the Patna–Delhi, Patna–Howrah and Barauni corridors;
(b) whether infrastructure constraints are affecting punctuality, freight movement and operational efficiency in the State;
(c) the measures taken to modernise signalling systems, eliminate bottlenecks and improve terminal capacity in Bihar; and
(d) whether a long-term railway capacity enhancement plan has been formulated to meet future transportation demand in the State?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive security audit of critical Government digital infrastructure against Artificial Intelligence-enabled cyber threats and ransomware attacks;
(b) whether vulnerabilities have been identified in digital public platforms and cloud-based Government services;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen cyber resilience, threat intelligence and incident response capabilities; and
(d) whether a national framework is under preparation to secure Government digital infrastructure against emerging cyber risks?

(a) whether Government has strengthened bilateral and multilateral engagements to secure reliable access to critical minerals essential for clean energy, semiconductor manufacturing and defence production;
(b) the countries with which India has entered into strategic partnerships for sourcing critical minerals;
(c) whether geopolitical developments have affected India's long-term mineral security strategy; and
(d) the measures taken to safeguard India's supply chains for strategically important minerals?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the effectiveness of disaster preparedness and emergency response mechanisms in flood-prone States, particularly Bihar, in view of increasingly frequent extreme rainfall events;
(b) whether coordination among the National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA), neighbouring States and Nepal has been strengthened for real-time flood forecasting and emergency response;
(c) the measures taken to improve evacuation planning, resilient communication systems and emergency logistics in vulnerable districts; and
(d) whether Government proposes to establish an integrated flood emergency management framework for the Ganga basin?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive review of cyber risks affecting India's rapidly expanding digital financial ecosystem, including banking, payment platforms and fintech services;
(b) whether increasing instances of AI-enabled financial frauds have necessitated strengthening the existing regulatory framework;
(c) the measures taken to improve coordination among financial regulators, banks and cyber security agencies for real-time threat response; and
(d) whether Government proposes to establish a unified national financial cyber security architecture to safeguard digital transactions?

(a) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of tertiary healthcare facilities in Bihar in view of the increasing patient load from neighbouring States;
(b) whether premier institutions located in Patna are adequately equipped to meet the growing demand for specialised medical treatment;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen advanced diagnostic, critical care and trauma management infrastructure in Bihar; and
(d) whether Government proposes to prepare a long-term healthcare infrastructure plan for eastern India with Bihar as a regional referral hub?

(a) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of domestic coal production and transportation to meet peak electricity demand during extreme weather conditions;
(b) whether coal evacuation infrastructure has kept pace with production growth in major coal-bearing States;
(c) the measures taken to improve supply chain efficiency and reduce logistical bottlenecks; and
(d) whether a long-term strategy has been formulated to ensure uninterrupted coal availability for critical sectors?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive assessment of increasing passenger and freight congestion at Patna Junction, Danapur, Rajendra Nagar Terminal and adjoining railway sections in view of the growing traffic demand in Bihar;
(b) whether infrastructure constraints have affected punctuality, operational efficiency and freight movement on the Delhi–Howrah corridor passing through Bihar;
(c) the measures taken to modernise signalling systems, expand terminal capacity and improve rail connectivity in the Patna region; and
(d) whether Government proposes to formulate a long-term infrastructure plan for enhancing railway capacity across Bihar to meet future transportation requirements?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the impact of changing global trade patterns and tariff measures on India's export competitiveness;
(b) the sectors identified as having significant opportunities under the evolving global supply chain;
(c) the measures taken to enhance India's manufacturing competitiveness and diversify export markets; and
(d) whether a strategic roadmap has been prepared to strengthen India's position in global value chains?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the safety and evacuation preparedness for Indian citizens residing in regions affected by armed conflicts and political instability;
(b) whether Indian Missions abroad have updated contingency and emergency response protocols for such situations;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen coordination with host Governments for ensuring the safety of Indian nationals; and
(d) whether Government proposes to establish a comprehensive digital emergency response mechanism for Indian citizens overseas?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a comprehensive assessment of the increasing incidence of cyber frauds, ransomware attacks and cross-border cyber threats affecting citizens, financial institutions and critical infrastructure;
(b) whether a coordinated national mechanism exists for real-time information sharing among Central agencies, States and financial regulators;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen digital forensic capabilities and cybercrime investigation across the country; and
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce additional safeguards to counter emerging cyber threats powered by Artificial Intelligence?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of Artificial Intelligence tools on examinations, academic research and learning outcomes in higher educational institutions;
(b) whether national guidelines are proposed for the ethical and responsible use of AI in education;
(c) the measures taken to prevent plagiarism, misuse of AI-generated content and compromise of academic standards; and
(d) whether Universities have been advised to develop institutional frameworks for responsible integration of emerging technologies?

(a) whether Government has recently reviewed the country's preparedness to detect and respond to emerging infectious diseases and zoonotic outbreaks;
(b) whether surveillance laboratories, genomic sequencing facilities and disease reporting systems have been strengthened across States;
(c) the measures taken to improve coordination between Central and State health authorities during public health emergencies; and
(d) whether any national framework has been developed for strengthening epidemic preparedness in view of changing disease patterns?
BPN

(a) whether Government has received complaints regarding harassment, intimidation and misbehaviour by bank officials and loan recovery agents while recovering loans from borrowers, including those in Bihar;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the compliance of banks with the guidelines issued by the banking regulator on fair recovery practices;
(c) the number of complaints received and action taken against banks and recovery agencies during the last three years; and
(d) whether Government proposes to strengthen safeguards and accountability to protect borrowers from coercive recovery practices?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the adequacy of interstate transmission infrastructure supplying electricity to Bihar in view of increasing industrial and urban demand; 
(b) whether transmission constraints have affected power reliability in Patna and adjoining districts; 
(c) the measures taken to improve grid resilience against extreme weather events; and 
(d) whether additional high-capacity transmission corridors are proposed to meet future electricity demand in Bihar?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a fresh assessment of recurring floods in the Ganga, Kosi, Gandak and Bagmati river basins affecting large parts of the State of Bihar during the current monsoon season;
(b) whether updated hydrological models and real-time data-sharing mechanisms with neighbouring countries have improved flood forecasting in the State;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen embankment safety, reservoir coordination and basin-level flood management; and
(d) whether Government proposes to formulate a long-term integrated river basin strategy to minimise recurring flood damage in the State of Bihar?

(a) the number of unorganised workers from Bihar registered on e-Shram portal since its nationwide expansion;
(b) whether workers from Patna district have received benefits such as accident insurance and social security coverage through the platform;
(c) whether any assessment has been done regarding gaps in awareness or enrolment among informal sector workers; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen labour welfare delivery systems and ensure effective coverage of vulnerable workers in urban areas of the State?

(a) the progress achieved under the national 4G saturation programme in uncovered villages of Bihar since 2023;
(b) whether Patna and surrounding districts have been included in deployment of indigenous 5G networks developed under national telecom initiatives;
(c) the financial assistance provided for strengthening telecom infrastructure and improving broadband connectivity in the State; and
(d) the steps taken to bridge the digital divide and ensure reliable high-speed connectivity for citizens, educational institutions and businesses in Patna?

(a) the number of schools in Bihar selected under the PM SHRI (Prime Minister Schools for Rising India) initiative since its launch and the number operational in Patna district;
(b) whether these schools have been equipped with modern laboratories, smart classrooms, skill training facilities and digital infrastructure in line with National Education Policy objectives;
(c) the total funds sanctioned and released for upgradation of educational infrastructure in Bihar under the scheme during 2023–26; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure equitable distribution of such model schools in rural and underdeveloped districts of the State?
v

(a) the total number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) functioning in Bihar and the number that have been computerised under the national PACS modernisation programme since 2023;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the effectiveness of digitalisation in improving transparency, credit delivery and service efficiency for farmers in districts, including Patna;
(c) the financial assistance sanctioned and utilised by Bihar under the Central scheme for computerisation and strengthening of PACS during the last three years; and
(d) the measures taken to promote diversification of PACS into multipurpose cooperative institutions offering services such as storage, fertilizer distribution, input supply and marketing support?

(a) the number of water bodies in Patna district restored under Mission Amrit Sarovar since its launch;
(b) whether these interventions have contributed to groundwater recharge and urban flood mitigation;
(c) the financial assistance provided to the State of Bihar for water conservation projects during 2023–26; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen long-term urban water security in Patna through integrated planning and community participation?

(a) the number of PACS in Bihar selected under the Grain Storage Plan launched in the year 2023;
(b) the storage capacity created or under construction in Patna district;
(c) the total funds allocated and utilised for cooperative-level storage infrastructure in the State; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of decentralised storage on reducing post-harvest losses and improving farmer incomes in Bihar?

(a) the number of Ayushman Arogya Mandirs (AAMs) operationalised in Bihar since the scheme’s expansion in 2023;
(b) whether urban primary health centres in Patna have been upgraded under this initiative;
(c) the financial assistance provided for strengthening diagnostic and telemedicine facilities; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure availability of trained medical personnel and essential medicines in upgraded health centres?
bpn

(a) the number of informal micro-enterprises in Patna registered under the Udyam Assist Platform since its launch in 2023;
(b) whether such enterprises have gained access to formal credit and Government procurement opportunities;
(c) the financial assistance provided under CGTMSE and other schemes to these units; and
(d) the steps taken to improve awareness, digital literacy and cluster-based support for small businesses in the State of Bihar?

(a) whether Patna has been included under the PM e-Bus Sewa scheme launched to promote electric public transport in urban centres;
(b) the number of electric buses sanctioned, delivered and operational in Patna under the scheme since 2023;
(c) the financial assistance provided by the Centre for charging infrastructure, depot modernisation and operational subsidies; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure long-term financial sustainability, reduction of urban air pollution and improvement in last-mile connectivity in the State capital?
BPN

(a) whether Patna Junction has been included under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS) launched in 2023 for large-scale modernisation of railway stations;
(b) the total project cost sanctioned, stage of implementation and expected completion timeline;
(c) whether passenger amenities such as waiting halls, lifts, escalators, accessibility features and integrated transport connectivity are being upgraded; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure minimal disruption to daily commuters during redevelopment and enhance passenger capacity in view of increasing footfall from Bihar?

(a) whether Bihar has been considered for inclusion or linkage benefits under the Pradhan Mantri Mega Integrated Textile Region and Apparel (PM MITRA) Parks Scheme;
(b) the support extended to textile units and handloom clusters in the State during 2023–26;
(c) whether employment generation targets have been fixed for eastern parts of the country under the scheme; and
(d) the steps taken to modernise Bihar’s traditional textile sector and integrate it into national supply chains?
bk

(a) the number of micro food processing units in Bihar supported under the PM Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) scheme since 2023;
(b) whether Patna and surrounding districts have been identified for cluster-based development of agro-processing units;
(c) the total financial assistance sanctioned and disbursed to beneficiaries in Bihar under credit-linked subsidies and seed capital support; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen value addition, cold chain infrastructure and market linkage support for small food processing entrepreneurs in the State?

(a) whether any institutions from Bihar, including universities in Patna, have been selected under the National Quantum Mission (NQM) for development of quantum communication, computing or sensing technologies;
(b) the funds allocated and research grants sanctioned to institutions in eastern India under the Mission since 2023;
(c) whether Government proposes to establish regional quantum research hubs to reduce geographical imbalance; and
(d) the steps taken to promote industry–academia collaboration and skill development in advanced technologies in the State?

(a) the number of workers registered on e-Shram portal in Bihar and the details of social security benefits extended to them;
(b) whether implementation of Labour Codes has improved worker protections in urban centres such as Patna;
(c) the training initiatives undertaken under Mission Karmayogi for labour administration in Bihar; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen grievance redressal and ensure timely delivery of worker welfare benefits?

(a) the status of implementation of Mission Lifestyle For Environment (LiFE) in Bihar and awareness campaigns conducted in Patna district;
(b) whether measurable reductions in plastic use, energy consumption and waste generation have been recorded;
(c) the funds allocated for climate adaptation and green urban initiatives in the State during the period from 2023 to 2026; and
(d) the steps taken to integrate Mission LiFE objectives with State-level urban planning and environmental management strategies?

(a) the total number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) in Bihar and those computerised during the last five years, along with the number of farmer-members benefited;
(b) the details of PACS converted into multipurpose societies and the range of services presently offered such as retail, storage, input supply and agri-services;
(c) the funds allocated, released and utilised in Bihar under the cooperative grain-storage initiative during 2024–26; and
(d) whether Government has reviewed diversification outcomes of PACS in Bihar and the steps taken to improve viability, digital integration and farmer outreach?

(a) whether complaints regarding biometric failures, exclusion of eligible beneficiaries and irregular functioning of Fair Price Shops (FPSs) have been reported from Patna city;
(b) the number of inspections conducted and action taken against erring dealers during the last three years;
(c) whether One Nation One Ration Card portability has benefited migrant populations in Patna; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen transparency, grievance redressal and efficiency of the urban PDS in Bihar?

(a) the current status of the Patna Smart City projects, specifically the integrated drainage and sewerage system upgrades mandated to be completed by 2026;
(b) whether the Central Government is providing technical or financial assistance for the Right to Walk initiative recently announced under Bihar’s Saat Nishchay-3 (Ease of Living) program in Patna;
(c) the details of funds sanctioned for the construction of escalators and foot-over bridges (FOBs) in high-congestion zones like Gandhi Maidan and Boring Road; and
(d) the timeline for the reclamation of 25 acres of Bihar Housing Cooperative land in the Rajiv Nagar-Digha area for urban redevelopment?

(a) whether small and marginal farmers in Bihar face difficulties in accessing organised markets and obtaining remunerative prices for their produce;
(b) the number of Farmer Producer Organisations (FPOs) functioning in Patna and adjoining districts;
(c) whether support for post-harvest infrastructure, storage and market linkage has been provided; and
(d) the steps taken to enhance farm income, reduce distress sales and strengthen market access for farmers in the State?

(a) whether handloom and textile workers in Bihar are facing livelihood challenges due to rising input costs, reduced demand and limited market access;
(b) the assistance provided to weavers in Patna region under central handloom and textile schemes;
(c) whether design development, marketing support and credit facilities have reached the intended beneficiaries; and
(d) the steps taken to revive traditional textile crafts and ensure sustainable income for artisans in the State?

(a) whether Bihar continues to lag behind other States in attracting large-scale industrial investment and manufacturing projects;
(b) the number of industrial projects approved or facilitated in Bihar during the last three years;
(c) whether infrastructure, logistics or regulatory constraints have been identified as the limiting factors; and
(d) the steps taken to improve 'Ease of Doing Business' and promote industrial and MSME growth in Bihar?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the research funding and laboratory infrastructure in universities and research institutions in Bihar;
(b) the details of financial assistance provided to institutions in Patna under various science and technology schemes during the last three years;
(c) whether innovation, incubation and industry–academia collaboration initiatives have been promoted; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen research capacity, encourage innovation and retain scientific talent in the State?

(a) whether the tourism potential of Patna, including religious, cultural and river-based tourism along the Ganga, has been assessed;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned for Patna under Swadesh Darshan, PRASHAD or other central schemes;
(c) whether gaps exist in connectivity, accommodation and tourist facilities; and
(d) the steps taken to develop sustainable tourism infrastructure and generate local employment opportunities in Bihar?
v

(a) whether skill training programmes implemented in Patna are translating into sustainable employment or self-employment opportunities for trained youth;
(b) the number of skill development centres functioning in Patna district under various central schemes;
(c) the placement outcomes achieved during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to align skill training curricula with local industry demand and emerging employment sectors in Bihar?

(a) whether a significant number of urban poor, street vendors and informal workers in Patna remain outside formal banking, insurance and credit systems;
(b) the number of beneficiaries covered under PM Jan Dhan Yojana, 
Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY) and Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY) in Patna district;
(c) whether issues relating to dormant accounts, limited financial literacy and restricted access to institutional credit have been identified; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen financial inclusion and expand affordable credit access for vulnerable urban populations in Bihar?

(a) whether parts of Patna face drinking water shortages and quality issues, particularly during summer months;
(b) the projects sanctioned for Patna under Jal Jeevan Mission (Urban) or other central water supply schemes;
(c) whether contamination of groundwater or pipeline leakages have been reported; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure safe, adequate and sustainable drinking water supply to the growing urban population of Patna?

(a) whether delays in wage payments under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) have been reported in Bihar, including in Patna district;
(b) the average time taken for wage disbursement during the last three years;
(c) whether quality and durability of assets created under the scheme have been reviewed; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure timely wage payments, strengthen monitoring and improve the long term utility of MGNREGS assets in the State?

(a) whether Government is aware that a large section of urban workers in Patna, particularly those engaged in construction, transport and service sectors, remain outside comprehensive social security coverage;
(b) the number of workers registered on e-Shram portal in Patna district and the benefits extended to them, so far;
(c) whether complaints regarding non-payment of wages, lack of insurance cover and unsafe working conditions have been received; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen the enforcement of labour laws, expand social security schemes and improve welfare delivery for unorganised and migrant workers in urban Bihar?

(a) whether Universities and colleges in Bihar, including those located in Patna, are facing shortages of regular teaching faculty;
(b) the present vacancy position in Central and Centrally funded institutions in the State;
(c) whether issues relating to student–teacher ratio and accreditation outcomes have been reviewed; and
(d) the steps taken to fill vacancies, strengthen academic governance and improve the quality of higher education in Bihar?

(a) whether Government hospitals and medical colleges in Patna are experiencing excessive patient load due to referrals from neighbouring districts and shortage of facilities in surrounding regions;
(b) whether shortages of doctors, nursing staff, beds, medicines and diagnostic equipment have been reported in major public hospitals;
(c) the funds allocated and released for strengthening healthcare infrastructure in Patna during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to expand hospital capacity, improve service delivery and reduce overcrowding in public health institutions in the capital city of Bihar?

(a) whether Government is aware that several residential and commercial areas of Patna faces severe waterlogging every year during the monsoon due to inadequate drainage infrastructure;
(b) the details of projects sanctioned for Patna under AMRUT, Smart Cities Mission or other Central schemes for improvement of drainage and sewerage systems;
(c) whether delays, design deficiencies or implementation gaps have been identified in execution of these projects; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure time-bound completion of urban drainage works and adoption of sustainable storm-water management solutions to prevent recurring hardship faced by the residents?

(a) whether Jay Prakash Narayan International airport at Patna, is experiencing congestion due to rising passenger traffic and limited terminal capacity;
(b) whether assessments have been conducted regarding peak-hour congestion, apron capacity and passenger amenities;
(c) the status of expansion or modernisation works undertaken at the airport during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to enhance air connectivity, passenger comfort and operational efficiency at Patna airport in view of its strategic importance for the State of Bihar?

(a) whether the level crossing at Phulwari Sharif, located behind Jay Prakash Narayan International Airport, Patna, has remained closed for several months for the construction of a proposed railway underpass;
(b) whether the tender process for the said underpass has already been completed and administrative approvals obtained;
(c) the reasons for non-commencement of construction work despite prolonged closure causing severe inconvenience to residents, school children, emergency services and commercial traffic; and
(d) the timeline by which construction of the railway underpass is likely to commence and to be completed to restore normal connectivity in the area?

(a) whether courts in Patna are witnessing high pendency of civil and criminal cases affecting the timely delivery of justice;
(b) the sanctioned strength versus the working strength of judges in district and subordinate courts there;
(c) whether shortages of courtrooms, support staff and digital infrastructure have been identified; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen judicial infrastructure, fill vacancies and promote speedy disposal of cases in the State capital?

(a) whether increasing traffic congestion and accident-prone stretches have been identified on National Highways and major arterial roads passing through Patna;
(b) the number of road accidents and fatalities reported in the district during the last three years;
(c) whether road safety audits, junction redesign and signage improvements have been undertaken; and
(d) the steps taken to improve traffic flow, pedestrian safety and coordination with the State authorities for urban road management?

(a) whether Government hospitals and medical colleges in Patna, including Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY) institutions, are facing shortages of doctors, nurses and critical medical equipments;
(b) the present vacancy position in such institutions;
(c) the funds released for strengthening tertiary healthcare infrastructure in Bihar during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure quality and affordable healthcare services in urban Bihar?

(a) whether urban poor households and informal workers in Patna face difficulties in accessing institutional credit;
(b) the number of beneficiaries covered under PMJDY, PMJJBY and PMSBY in Patna district;
(c) whether any assessment has been made regarding exclusion from formal financial systems; and
(d) the steps taken to deepen financial inclusion in urban areas of Bihar?

(a) whether urban local bodies in Patna are facing recurring problems of waterlogging and urban flooding during monsoon due to inadequate drainage infrastructure and Ganga river backflow;
(b) whether any comprehensive drainage and flood mitigation project has been sanctioned for Patna under AMRUT, Smart Cities Mission or any other Central Scheme;
(c) the funds released and works completed so far for stormwater drainage in Patna during the last five years; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure long-term, climate-resilient urban infrastructure for flood-prone cities in the State of Bihar?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the availability of mobile towers and 5G coverage in Patna, Gaya, Nalanda and rural blocks of Bihar;
(b) the details of villages which are still lacking reliable telecom connectivity despite the BharatNet and USOF programmes; and
(c) the steps being taken to establish new telecom infrastructure, especially in Left Wing Extremism affected and remote pockets?

(a) what steps have been introduced to restructure cooperative societies in the State of Bihar, aiming to enhance rural economic outputs;
(b) how effective the training and Government subsidies have been in improving operational transparency and member engagement; and
(c) what challenges remain and what new policies are underway to ensure the financial stability of cooperatives?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of rising complaints regarding fraudulent practices during car-insurance claim settlement, including coercive assessment, arbitrary deductions and forced cash-loss agreements by insurers or surveyors;
(b) the steps taken by IRDAI to strengthen monitoring of motor-claim investigations, digital evidence verification and grievance redressal;
(c) whether stricter penalties for surveyor misconduct are being considered; and
(d) the details of actions taken against insurers found violating claim-settlement norms over the last three years?

(a) whether Government has assessed project-wise bottlenecks affecting coal evacuation from mines adjoining the Bihar–Jharkhand region;
(b) steps taken to expand mechanised loading, first-mile connectivity and dedicated railway corridors;
(c) whether new washeries are being planned; and
(d) details of funds sanctioned for production modernisation during the last two years?

(a) whether Government has evaluated the mobile tower density and connectivity gaps in rural Bihar;
(b) the district-wise status of 5G rollout in the State, as of November 2025; and
(c) the measures for high-speed internet availability in far-flung villages and border areas?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed district-wise progress of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACSs) computerisation in Bihar upto October, 2025, including functioning of new workflow and payment modules;
(b) the steps taken to convert PACS into multi-service centres offering storage, retail, agricultural inputs and doorstep financial services to farmers; and
(c) the funds sanctioned under national cooperative infrastructure strengthening and digitisation initiatives?

(a) whether the Ministry has conducted a comprehensive assessment of shortages related to permanent faculty, advanced laboratories, hostels and research facilities across State Universities and colleges in Bihar;
(b) the status of grants released under PM-USHA, RUSA and HEFA during financial year 2024–25 for infrastructure upgrade; and
(c) the steps taken to promote digital classrooms, incubation centres, interdisciplinary research and skill-oriented academic programmes?

(a) whether Government has examined irregularities in fertilizer retailing, overcharging and PoS-based verification across districts of the State of Bihar;
(b) the steps taken to ensure real-time fertilizer supply-chain tracking, stock visibility and dealer accountability; and
(c) the measures introduced to improve subsidy transparency, reduce diversion and strengthen monitoring during peak agricultural seasons?

